{"questions":[{"question_id":"lv40va43","content":"<p>Identify the incorrect statements about group 15 elements :</p>\n<p>(A) Dinitrogen is a diatomic gas which acts like an inert gas at room temperature.</p>\n<p>(B) The common oxidation states of these elements are <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.789ex\" height=\"1.943ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 3000.7 859\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><use data-c=\"2C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1722.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2500.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and +5.</p>\n<p>(C) Nitrogen has unique ability to form <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.874ex\" height=\"1.758ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 3480.4 777\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(556,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1351.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2351.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2907.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> multiple bonds.</p>\n<p>(D) The stability of +5 oxidation states increases down the group.</p>\n<p>(E) Nitrogen shows a maximum covalency of 6.</p>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-8th-april-evening-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift","permalink":"pidentify-the-incorrect-statements-about-group-15-elements-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-gghx38o3j7eo73ym","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Identify the incorrect statements about group 15 elements :</p>\n<p>(A) Dinitrogen is a diatomic gas which acts like an inert gas at room temperature.</p>\n<p>(B) The common oxidation states of these elements are <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.789ex\" height=\"1.943ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 3000.7 859\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><use data-c=\"2C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1722.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2500.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and +5.</p>\n<p>(C) Nitrogen has unique ability to form <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.874ex\" height=\"1.758ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 3480.4 777\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(556,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1351.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2351.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2907.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> multiple bonds.</p>\n<p>(D) The stability of +5 oxidation states increases down the group.</p>\n<p>(E) Nitrogen shows a maximum covalency of 6.</p>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"(A), (C), (E) only\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"(D) and (E) only\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"(A), (B), (D) only\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"(B), (D), (E) only"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Let's analyze each statement step by step to identify the incorrect ones:</p>\n\n<p>(A) Dinitrogen is a diatomic gas which acts like an inert gas at room temperature.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is generally correct. Dinitrogen (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.804ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1239.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(836,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is indeed a diatomic gas and is very inert at room temperature due to the strong triple bond between the nitrogen atoms.</p>\n\n<p>(B) The common oxidation states of these elements are <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.789ex\" height=\"1.943ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 3000.7 859\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><use data-c=\"2C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1722.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2500.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and +5.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is also correct. The group 15 elements commonly exhibit oxidation states of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.891ex\" height=\"1.69ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 1278 747\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (in nitrides), <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.891ex\" height=\"1.69ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 1278 747\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (as in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>), and +5 (as in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.142ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2714.6 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"4F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4F\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2311,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>).</p>\n\n<p>(C) Nitrogen has unique ability to form <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.874ex\" height=\"1.758ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 3480.4 777\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(556,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1351.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2351.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2907.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> multiple bonds.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is correct. Nitrogen has a unique ability to form <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.634ex\" height=\"1.758ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 3374.4 777\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(503,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1298.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2298.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2801.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> multiple bonds, which is why it can form a triple bond (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.804ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1239.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(836,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>).</p>\n\n<p>(D) The stability of +5 oxidation states increases down the group.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is incorrect. The stability of +5 oxidation states actually decreases down the group due to the effect of inert pair effect. For example, bismuth in +5 state is less stable than nitrogen in +5 state.</p>\n\n<p>(E) Nitrogen shows a maximum covalency of 6.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is incorrect. Nitrogen can exhibit a maximum covalency of 4 (as in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.69ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.826ex\" height=\"2.554ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 2133.1 1128.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-305.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>). It cannot expand its octet to show a covalency of 6.</p>\n\n<p>Based on the above analysis, the incorrect statements are (D) and (E). Therefore, the correct answer is:</p>\n\n<p>Option B: (D) and (E) only</p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>समूह 15 तत्वों के बारे में असत्य कथन को पहचानें :</p>\n<p>(A) डाइनाइट्रोजन एक द्विपरमाणुक गैस है जो कमरे के ताप पर अक्रिय गैस की भाँति कार्य करता है।</p>\n<p>(B) इन तत्वों की सामान्य ऑक्सीकरण अवस्थाएँ <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.789ex\" height=\"1.943ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 3000.7 859\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><use data-c=\"2C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1722.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2500.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> एवं +5 हैं।</p>\n<p>(C) नाइट्रोजन में <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.874ex\" height=\"1.758ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 3480.4 777\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(556,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1351.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2351.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2907.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बहुबन्ध बनाने की विशिष्ट योग्यता है।</p>\n<p>(D) ऑक्सीकरण संख्या +5 का स्थायित्व समूह में नीचे जाने पर बढ़ता है।</p>\n<p>(E) नाइट्रोजन 6 की अधिकतम सहसंयोजकता प्रदर्शित करता है।</p>\n<p>नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सही उत्तर चुने :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"केवल (A), (C), (E)"},{"identifier":"B","content":"केवल (D) एवं (E)\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"केवल (A), (B), (D)\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"केवल (B), (D), (E)\n"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>आइए प्रत्येक कथन का चरण-दर-चरण विश्लेषण करें और गलत कथनों की पहचान करें:</p>\n\n<p>(A) डाइनाइट्रोजन एक द्विपरमाणुक गैस है जो कमरे के तापमान पर अक्रिय गैस की तरह व्यवहार करती है।</p>\n\n<p>यह कथन सामान्यतः सही है। डाइनाइट्रोजन (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.804ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1239.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(836,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) वास्तव में एक द्विपरमाणुक गैस है और नाइट्रोजन परमाणुओं के बीच प्रबल त्रिबंध के कारण कमरे के तापमान पर बहुत अक्रिय है।</p>\n\n<p>(B) इन तत्वों की सामान्य ऑक्सीकरण अवस्थाएँ <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.789ex\" height=\"1.943ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 3000.7 859\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><use data-c=\"2C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1722.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2500.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> और +5 हैं।</p>\n\n<p>यह कथन भी सही है। समूह 15 के तत्व सामान्यतः <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.891ex\" height=\"1.69ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 1278 747\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (नाइट्राइड में), <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.891ex\" height=\"1.69ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 1278 747\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (जैसे <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> में), और +5 (जैसे <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.142ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2714.6 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"4F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4F\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2311,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> में) ऑक्सीकरण अवस्थाएँ प्रदर्शित करते हैं।</p>\n\n<p>(C) नाइट्रोजन में <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.874ex\" height=\"1.758ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 3480.4 777\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(556,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1351.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2351.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2907.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बहुबंध बनाने की अद्वितीय क्षमता है।</p>\n\n<p>यह कथन सही है। नाइट्रोजन में <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.634ex\" height=\"1.758ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 3374.4 777\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(503,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1298.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2298.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2801.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बहुबंध बनाने की अद्वितीय क्षमता है, यही कारण है कि यह त्रिबंध (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.804ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1239.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(836,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) बना सकता है।</p>\n\n<p>(D) समूह में नीचे जाने पर +5 ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था की स्थिरता बढ़ती है।</p>\n\n<p>यह कथन गलत है। अक्रिय युग्म प्रभाव के कारण समूह में नीचे जाने पर +5 ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था की स्थिरता वास्तव में घटती है। उदाहरण के लिए, +5 अवस्था में बिस्मथ, +5 अवस्था में नाइट्रोजन की तुलना में कम स्थिर है।</p>\n\n<p>(E) नाइट्रोजन अधिकतम 6 की सहसंयोजकता प्रदर्शित करता है।</p>\n\n<p>यह कथन गलत है। नाइट्रोजन अधिकतम 4 की सहसंयोजकता प्रदर्शित कर सकता है (जैसे <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.69ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.826ex\" height=\"2.554ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 2133.1 1128.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-305.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> में)। यह 6 की सहसंयोजकता दिखाने के लिए अपने अष्टक का विस्तार नहीं कर सकता।</p>\n\n<p>उपरोक्त विश्लेषण के आधार पर, गलत कथन (D) और (E) हैं। इसलिए, सही उत्तर है:</p>\n\n<p>विकल्प B: केवल (D) और (E)</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"group-15-elements-nitrogen-family","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["multi_statements"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-8th-april-evening-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"(A), (C), (E) only\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"(D) and (E) only\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"(A), (B), (D) only\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"(B), (D), (E) only"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>Let's analyze each statement step by step to identify the incorrect ones:</p>\n\n<p>(A) Dinitrogen is a diatomic gas which acts like an inert gas at room temperature.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is generally correct. Dinitrogen (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.804ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1239.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(836,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is indeed a diatomic gas and is very inert at room temperature due to the strong triple bond between the nitrogen atoms.</p>\n\n<p>(B) The common oxidation states of these elements are <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.789ex\" height=\"1.943ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 3000.7 859\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><use data-c=\"2C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1722.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2500.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and +5.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is also correct. The group 15 elements commonly exhibit oxidation states of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.891ex\" height=\"1.69ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 1278 747\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (in nitrides), <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.891ex\" height=\"1.69ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 1278 747\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (as in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>), and +5 (as in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.142ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2714.6 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"4F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4F\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2311,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>).</p>\n\n<p>(C) Nitrogen has unique ability to form <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.874ex\" height=\"1.758ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 3480.4 777\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(556,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1351.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2351.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2907.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> multiple bonds.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is correct. Nitrogen has a unique ability to form <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.634ex\" height=\"1.758ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 3374.4 777\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(503,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1298.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2298.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2801.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> multiple bonds, which is why it can form a triple bond (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.804ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1239.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(836,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>).</p>\n\n<p>(D) The stability of +5 oxidation states increases down the group.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is incorrect. The stability of +5 oxidation states actually decreases down the group due to the effect of inert pair effect. For example, bismuth in +5 state is less stable than nitrogen in +5 state.</p>\n\n<p>(E) Nitrogen shows a maximum covalency of 6.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is incorrect. Nitrogen can exhibit a maximum covalency of 4 (as in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.69ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.826ex\" height=\"2.554ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 2133.1 1128.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-305.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>). It cannot expand its octet to show a covalency of 6.</p>\n\n<p>Based on the above analysis, the incorrect statements are (D) and (E). Therefore, the correct answer is:</p>\n\n<p>Option B: (D) and (E) only</p>"}]}